/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# Lived at the repo root until 2026-09-01, which meant Cloudflare Pages never
# saw it: pages_build_output_dir is `dist`, Astro copies `public/` into it, and
# nothing copied a root-level file. Measured on the live origin at the time:
# /_astro/*.css returned `cache-control: public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate`
# - Pages' own 4-hour default - not the immutable rule below, and dist/_headers
# did not exist. The X-Robots-Tag rules under it had never applied either.
#
# Those noindex rules are kept, with their premise corrected. The comment they
# carried said Pages served the project from the repository root, so README.md,
# AGENTS.md and package.json returned 200. That is no longer true - all three
# return 404 now, because only dist/ is published - so the rules are insurance
# against the output directory changing back, not a live fix.
#
# scripts/validate/seo-surfaces.mjs now hard-fails if dist/_headers is missing
# or has lost the immutable rule, so this file cannot silently stop shipping.

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Pinterest RSS feed (data/pinterest/pinfeed.json). Pages would serve .xml as
# application/xml; Pinterest expects an RSS content type.
/pinfeed.xml
  Content-Type: application/rss+xml; charset=utf-8

# Caching (10 Nov 2026). Pages serve from Cloudflare's edge with no Function in front
# (public/_routes.json sends only /api/* and the pin feeds to Functions). HTML keeps Pages' own
# "max-age=0, must-revalidate": the browser re-checks with an ETag and gets a 304, so a deploy
# shows at once. No /* cache rule on purpose: Pages joins repeated headers with a comma, which
# would corrupt the immutable rule above.
#
# Files whose URL does not change when their content does: a day in the browser, served stale
# for up to a week while the new copy is fetched.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800
/samples/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/og.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

# Never cached: the page a buyer returns to from Stripe (its URL carries her checkout session).
/checkout/*
  Cache-Control: private, no-store

# Preview hosts duplicate the live site page for page and must never be indexed. This was done by
# the root middleware; pages no longer pass through it, so the rule lives here.
https://:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
https://preview.approvalprep.com/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
